WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.094 --> 00:00:03.551
- Checking out a bird mount, or a skull,

00:00:03.551 --> 00:00:07.137
or a fish mount is just
like checking out a book.

00:00:07.137 --> 00:00:11.313
You present your library
card, we scan it, it's due

00:00:11.313 --> 00:00:15.480
in two weeks, and it's just
like checking out a book.

00:00:17.096 --> 00:00:19.653
This is the Alaska resources
library and information

00:00:19.653 --> 00:00:23.602
services, and we're in the
room that holds the furs,

00:00:23.602 --> 00:00:26.064
mounts and skulls in our collection.

00:00:26.064 --> 00:00:30.038
Many of the items are
available for the public.

00:00:30.038 --> 00:00:33.860
- The focus of the collection
is Alaskan animals,

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.193
birds, and fish.

00:00:36.962 --> 00:00:39.962
I'd says there are hundreds of furs.

00:00:41.032 --> 00:00:45.032
Probably 50 bird mounts,
and hundreds of skulls.

00:00:46.839 --> 00:00:50.198
- This has a walrus skull,
which is kind of interesting.

00:00:50.198 --> 00:00:52.342
It's got teeth behind the tusks.

00:00:52.342 --> 00:00:54.257
I didn't realize that until
I got to look at the skull,

00:00:54.257 --> 00:00:55.452
it was pretty cool.

00:00:55.452 --> 00:00:56.934
(playful music)

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:59.470
- The bear furs are really popular,

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:01.720
well, bear, lynx, and wolf.

00:01:05.322 --> 00:01:09.489
When people encounter this
collection, they are delighted.

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:12.492
They ooh and ah.

00:01:12.492 --> 00:01:17.331
It sparks their imagination,
they love having all the choice

00:01:17.331 --> 00:01:21.509
of the different types
of items that we have.

00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:24.568
People who check out
these items really vary,

00:01:24.568 --> 00:01:28.168
mainly teachers, for their
Alaska animal component

00:01:28.168 --> 00:01:30.432
of their curriculum.

00:01:30.432 --> 00:01:33.918
- I don't know of anywhere
else that they can borrow

00:01:33.918 --> 00:01:38.085
a mounted sandhill crane
and just study it up close.

00:01:39.664 --> 00:01:42.081
It's a very unusual program.

